  "label": "User projected onto the group of professionals as 'people who were just doing their jobs'",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'person' (the diverse group of six professionals) through the textual message 'it happened because of people who were just doing their jobs'. The user identifies with or imagines themselves as part of this group, adopting the perspective of collective responsibility and apathy. This projection is implicit, not explicit, but is inferred from the meme's rhetorical device of deflecting accountability by attributing failure to a group rather than a single individual. The user sees themselves as part of the 'system' or 'organization' that failed, and thus identifies with the group's posture and demeanor.",
